{{!-- The srcset and sizes of a fluid photograph, written inside the <img> tag:

	<img src="{{img_url feature_image size="m"}}" {{> "image-srcset" image=feature_image sizes="(min-width: 768px) 460px, 100vw"}} …>

Every candidate is one of package.json's image_sizes, in WebP, so the browser picks the smallest
file that covers the slot at the screen's density. `ml` (800px) exists for phones: a ~372px card at
2x needs 744px, which 600 misses and 960 overshoots by a third. The `src` stays a JPEG at the size
the slot used to ask for, for anything that reads `src` alone.

`sizes` is the slot's rendered width, measured on every Layout of every Surface at 390, 768, 1024,
1440 and 1568px (DECISIONS.md, "Responsive images"). It errs wide, never narrow: a slot that says
460px and renders 480px fetches a slightly blurry image, one that says 480px and renders 460px
fetches a few kilobytes more.

Ghost resizes on request and never enlarges, so a 1200px original answers the 2000w candidate with
its own 1200px. An image Ghost does not host (an external URL) comes back unsized for every
candidate, and the browser downloads it once. --}}
srcset="{{img_url image size="s" format="webp"}} 320w, {{img_url image size="m" format="webp"}} 600w, {{img_url image size="ml" format="webp"}} 800w, {{img_url image size="l" format="webp"}} 960w, {{img_url image size="xl" format="webp"}} 1200w, {{img_url image size="xxl" format="webp"}} 2000w"
sizes="{{sizes}}"
